# Per-device runtime state, not configuration - the same reason
# data/account_labels.json is ignored above.
#
# This was tracked, and that was actively dangerous once the System page started
# storing the touchscreen calibration in it: a deploy would check out the
# developer's copy over the wall's, wiping a calibration someone had just done by
# tapping five crosshairs. Nothing else in the file belongs to the repo either -
# which calendars are hidden and which rail sections are switched off are decisions
# made on the wall, per wall.
#
# load_prefs() returns sane defaults when the file is absent, so a fresh clone
# needs nothing here.
data/calendar_prefs.json
